  "notes": "A fall through a doorway whose hazard is `fall`. A case gives the storey indexes (z) of the room the doorway leaves and the room it enters, the world's gravity (null for none), the falling body's abilities (null for a body with none) and the seed's story, playthrough, at (the story clock in epoch seconds) and sequence (the doorway's id); the seed's kind is the `kind` constant. storeys is how far the doorway goes down, null unless both rooms have a storey and the first is higher. dice is storeys times the gravity's dice, null when nothing is thrown (then there is nothing else). save is the d20 against fall_save thrown first (die null when the target is 0 or less), or null for a body with no abilities; rolled is the pool of fall_die thrown second out of the same generator; damage is rolled, halved and rounded down when the save passed; words is what the toll's sentences say the fall was.",
